# A close of a socket another thread waits on ends the wait at once, never
# after a slice (defect 2502, panel 248's R2, 2026-11-14). The layer's calls
# waited in slices of 50 ms, asking between them whether the socket was
# closed, so a close ended a waiting `accept` about 25 ms later on the median,
# 38 ms measured on Darwin, where a listener's shutdown wakes nothing; now the
# close wakes the waiting call itself, on every platform. Twenty accepts wait,
# each on a listener of its own, each listener is closed in turn, and the
# median of the times from a close to its accept's return is held under
# 10 ms, which slices of 50 ms pass with a chance near 1 in 400. The waiting
# threads are C's, in the header beside this file. It prints 1 where every
# step held, else the step that did not.
extern "fixedbugs-2502-waiters.h"
    function close_wakes_at_once(n: i64) -> i64

function main()
    print(f"twenty closes each end the accept waiting on them at once: {close_wakes_at_once(n: 20)}")
